blackpearl_datachannel links these libraries into its native library, built from their sources, each under its
authors' copyright and its own license:

libdatachannel 0.24.8 (Paul-Louis Ageneau and contributors)
  Mozilla Public License 2.0. Source: https://github.com/paullouisageneau/libdatachannel

libjuice (Paul-Louis Ageneau and contributors)
  Mozilla Public License 2.0. Source: https://github.com/paullouisageneau/libjuice

usrsctp (the usrsctp authors)
  BSD 3-Clause License. Source: https://github.com/sctplab/usrsctp, as forked at
  https://github.com/paullouisageneau/usrsctp

plog (Sergey Podobry and contributors)
  MIT License. Source: https://github.com/SergiusTheBest/plog

Mbed TLS 3.6.8 (the Mbed TLS Contributors)
  Apache License 2.0. Source: https://github.com/Mbed-TLS/mbedtls

The Mozilla Public License 2.0 is at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/, the Apache License 2.0 at
https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0. The exact commits used are in src/CMakeLists.txt.

